{
  "case_id": "2009-08-769",
  "document_hash": "44a17a618bcb25f0ba12459b7f600e58442daa0578e3fc6af294bb0bc9652ac2",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2009-08-769",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "44a17a618bcb25f0ba12459b7f600e58442daa0578e3fc6af294bb0bc9652ac2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-44a17a618bcb-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. KATYAL: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: Ten years ago, in Section 48 of Title 18, Congress crafted a narrowly targeted restriction against certain depictions of actual animal cruelty. Yet the Third Circuit struck the statute down on its face without even attempting to apply substantial overbreadth analysis. The statute has four critical features and, just as the Court last year in United States v. Williams began with statutory construction, analysis should begin there."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2009-08-769",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "44a17a618bcb25f0ba12459b7f600e58442daa0578e3fc6af294bb0bc9652ac2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-44a17a618bcb-0000-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: What record do you have of that fact?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-08-769",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "44a17a618bcb25f0ba12459b7f600e58442daa0578e3fc6af294bb0bc9652ac2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-44a17a618bcb-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: What do you mean by a \"for-profit commercial market\"? You mean anything that is sold, right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2009-08-769",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "44a17a618bcb25f0ba12459b7f600e58442daa0578e3fc6af294bb0bc9652ac2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-44a17a618bcb-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. KATYAL: That is -- that is correct."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2009-08-769",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "44a17a618bcb25f0ba12459b7f600e58442daa0578e3fc6af294bb0bc9652ac2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-44a17a618bcb-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 14,
        "start": 14
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Can you give me an example of a case where we said a statute which might otherwise be overbroad is not overbroad because prosecutors have been restrained? Can you give me one case where we've said that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2009-08-769",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "44a17a618bcb25f0ba12459b7f600e58442daa0578e3fc6af294bb0bc9652ac2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-44a17a618bcb-0000-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 14,
        "start": 14
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. KATYAL: Last year in United States v. Williams, an opinion that virtually every member of this Court joined, including you, Justice Kennedy, this Court said that it would look to the experience, the post-Ferber experience, in prosecuting cases to decide whether or not a -- two terms in the statute, \"promotes\" and \"presents,\" were vague and would raise the --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2009-08-769",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "44a17a618bcb25f0ba12459b7f600e58442daa0578e3fc6af294bb0bc9652ac2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-44a17a618bcb-0000-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 15,
        "start": 15
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: But what is a -- what is \"and the like\"? How about cockfighting? What is the difference between -- perhaps I missed something a few moments ago -- between bullfighting, cockfighting, dogfighting? You say dogfighting is included, but bullfighting -- and I don't know where you put cockfighting."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2009-08-769",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "44a17a618bcb25f0ba12459b7f600e58442daa0578e3fc6af294bb0bc9652ac2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-44a17a618bcb-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Why? Why? You say a crush video, my description that I read of it, you would have a strong case. I'm not saying you would win, I don't have to decide that. But you have a very strong case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2009-08-769",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "44a17a618bcb25f0ba12459b7f600e58442daa0578e3fc6af294bb0bc9652ac2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-44a17a618bcb-0001-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF PATRICIA A. MILLETT ON BEHALF OF THE RESPONDENT"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Millett",
      "case_id": "2009-08-769",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "44a17a618bcb25f0ba12459b7f600e58442daa0578e3fc6af294bb0bc9652ac2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-44a17a618bcb-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. MILLETT: I think -- I think there's a -- that a properly drawn law could very well, at least in my humble opinion, this Court would have to decide, survive strict scrutiny. There is also, I suppose, some argument whether it would fit into -- you wouldn't need strict scrutiny, you would fit it into an unprotected category of speech like obscenity or it would be the production issue that would -- like you have in Ferber."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2009-08-769",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "44a17a618bcb25f0ba12459b7f600e58442daa0578e3fc6af294bb0bc9652ac2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-44a17a618bcb-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Does this -- would this record support any ban? I mean, there was a real concentration on crush videos. So there is that. Is there anything else in the current record other than the crush videos?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2009-08-769",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "44a17a618bcb25f0ba12459b7f600e58442daa0578e3fc6af294bb0bc9652ac2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-44a17a618bcb-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: But in determining whether this is over -- overly broad, do we -- do we think of all of the hypotheticals that we possibly can think of that might fall within this statute: somebody hunting in the District of Columbia, somebody producing fois gras with a goose and say, \"Well, we've thought of a lot of hypothetical situations where this statute might apply and therefore it's overly broad\"? Or do we look at what's going on in the real world?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2009-08-769",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "44a17a618bcb25f0ba12459b7f600e58442daa0578e3fc6af294bb0bc9652ac2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-44a17a618bcb-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. MILLETT: I think what you do is you look at text of the statute, and then you ask yourself, how much of a strain is it to come up with a factual pattern that will fit into it? In Williams you had to first of all read the --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2009-08-769",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "44a17a618bcb25f0ba12459b7f600e58442daa0578e3fc6af294bb0bc9652ac2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-44a17a618bcb-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: What do you mean by \"even-handed,\" please? I'm not -- you are using those words. What do you mean about \"even-handed and narrowly tailored\"?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-08-769",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "44a17a618bcb25f0ba12459b7f600e58442daa0578e3fc6af294bb0bc9652ac2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-44a17a618bcb-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: I don't understand. Are you saying, since there is no human sacrifice in this country and no market to be dried up, the videos would be okay?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Katyal",
      "case_id": "2009-08-769",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "44a17a618bcb25f0ba12459b7f600e58442daa0578e3fc6af294bb0bc9652ac2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-44a17a618bcb-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. KATYAL: I'm saying that, if Congress identified a market and if a video -- if the snuff video market was driving, somehow, people to get killed, Congress would be fully within its power to regulate it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2009-08-769",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "44a17a618bcb25f0ba12459b7f600e58442daa0578e3fc6af294bb0bc9652ac2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-44a17a618bcb-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: How many prosecutions have there been for crush videos?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Katyal",
      "case_id": "2009-08-769",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "44a17a618bcb25f0ba12459b7f600e58442daa0578e3fc6af294bb0bc9652ac2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-44a17a618bcb-0003-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. KATYAL: There -- there haven't been any prosecutions for crush videos, and I think the reason is because the market dried up very quickly after the enactment of Section 48."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2009-08-769",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "44a17a618bcb25f0ba12459b7f600e58442daa0578e3fc6af294bb0bc9652ac2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-44a17a618bcb-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Did I just understand you to agree with your colleague on the other side, that Congress could not ban the human sacrifice channel because there would be no connection between drying up the underlying activity?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Katyal",
      "case_id": "2009-08-769",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "44a17a618bcb25f0ba12459b7f600e58442daa0578e3fc6af294bb0bc9652ac2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-44a17a618bcb-0003-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. KATYAL: I think that does start to reach into questions about obscenity and expressive impact on viewers, which is not before this Court."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-08-769",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "44a17a618bcb25f0ba12459b7f600e58442daa0578e3fc6af294bb0bc9652ac2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-44a17a618bcb-0003-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: How about the statute's term, \"kill\" --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2009-08-769",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "44a17a618bcb25f0ba12459b7f600e58442daa0578e3fc6af294bb0bc9652ac2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-44a17a618bcb-0003-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel, both counsel, for very able presentation. The case is submitted.\n(Whereupon, at 11:06 a.m., the case in the above-entitled matter was submitted.)"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2009-08-769",
